IMPORT prelude

-- Limitation Act 1959 (Singapore) -- the main limitation periods (ss 6, 6A, 9, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24A, 24B), disability
-- (s 24), acknowledgment and part payment (ss 26 to 28), fraud and mistake (s 29), pleading (s 4), and the occupation
-- years (s 35).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/LA1959.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 20 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository (ss 6 and 33 by 4 each), and it governs
-- every civil claim that has no limitation period of its own. Nearly the whole Act is encoded; it is 44,000 characters.
-- Not encoded: the detailed accrual rules for land and future interests (ss 10 to 14, 17), trusts of land (s 12), revenue
-- sales (s 8), the transitional sections, and s 33 beyond its tax exclusion.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation Act 1959 -- periods`

§§ `3, 4 -- when the Act applies`

-- s 3: the Act does not apply where another written law prescribes a period. s 4: "Nothing in this Act shall operate as a bar
-- to an action unless this Act has been EXPRESSLY PLEADED as a defence". A defendant who does not plead limitation loses it.
GIVEN `the claim is out of time` IS A BOOLEAN, `limitation was pleaded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is barred` IF
    `the claim is out of time` AND `limitation was pleaded`

§§ `6, 6A, 9, 20 to 23 -- the periods`

-- s 6(1): contract, tort, recognizances, awards, sums recoverable under statute -- 6 YEARS from accrual. (2): account -- 6.
-- (3): an action on a JUDGMENT -- 12 years; judgment interest -- 6. (4): a statutory PENALTY or forfeiture -- ONE year.
-- s 6A: CONTRIBUTION between wrongdoers -- 2 years from the judgment, award, or agreed settlement fixing the payer's liability.
-- s 9(1): recovery of LAND -- 12 years (but (2) not against a proprietor registered under the Land Titles Act 1993).
-- s 20: arrears of rent -- 6. s 21(1): principal secured by mortgage, or sale proceeds -- 12; (6) mortgage interest -- 6.
-- s 23: a share of a deceased person's personal estate -- 12; arrears of interest on a legacy -- 6.
DECLARE ClaimType IS ONE OF
    `contract`
    `tort other than personal injury`
    `personal injury`
    `enforcing a judgment`
    `a statutory penalty`
    `contribution from a co-wrongdoer`
    `recovering unregistered land`
    `arrears of rent`
    `mortgage principal`
    `a share of a deceased's estate`
    `breach of trust`

-- In years.
GIVEN `the claim` IS A ClaimType
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the primary period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `contract` THEN 6
    WHEN `tort other than personal injury` THEN 6
    WHEN `personal injury` THEN 3
    WHEN `enforcing a judgment` THEN 12
    WHEN `a statutory penalty` THEN 1
    WHEN `contribution from a co-wrongdoer` THEN 2
    WHEN `recovering unregistered land` THEN 12
    WHEN `arrears of rent` THEN 6
    WHEN `mortgage principal` THEN 12
    WHEN `a share of a deceased's estate` THEN 12
    WHEN `breach of trust` THEN 6

§§ `22 -- trusts`

-- s 22(1): NO period applies to an action by a beneficiary "(a) in respect of any fraud or fraudulent breach of trust to which
-- the trustee was a party or privy; or (b) to recover from the trustee trust property ... in the possession of the trustee, or
-- previously received by the trustee and converted to his use". (2): otherwise 6 years.
GIVEN `trustee party to fraud` IS A BOOLEAN, `trustee holds or converted the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no limitation period applies against the trustee` IF
    `trustee party to fraud` OR `trustee holds or converted the property`

§§ `24A, 24B -- negligence and latent damage`

-- s 24A(2): negligence, nuisance or breach of duty claims for PERSONAL INJURIES -- the later of (a) 3 years from accrual or (b)
-- 3 years from the claimant's "knowledge". (3): other such claims -- the later of (a) 6 years from accrual or (b) 3 years from
-- knowledge. (4): knowledge means of the attribution, the defendant's identity, and material facts making the injury serious
-- enough to sue; (5) knowledge that it was legally negligent is irrelevant; (6) includes what reasonable inquiry and expert
-- advice would reveal.
-- s 24B(1): "shall not be brought after the expiration of 15 YEARS from the starting date" (the last negligent act), and (3)
-- "notwithstanding that the cause of action has not yet accrued".
--
-- The 15-year longstop can bar a claim before damage has even occurred: a building defect that causes damage in year 16 never
-- gives a claim.
DECLARE Negligence HAS
    `personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years since accrual` IS A NUMBER
    `years since knowledge` IS A NUMBER
    `years since the negligent act` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Negligence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the negligence claim is in time` IF
        `the claim`'s `years since the negligent act` AT MOST 15
    AND (IF `the claim`'s `personal injury`
         THEN `the claim`'s `years since accrual` AT MOST 3 OR `the claim`'s `years since knowledge` AT MOST 3
         ELSE `the claim`'s `years since accrual` AT MOST 6 OR `the claim`'s `years since knowledge` AT MOST 3)

§§ `24 -- disability`

-- s 24(1): if the claimant was under a disability (a minor, or lacking capacity under the Mental Capacity Act -- s 2(2)) when
-- the right accrued, the action may be brought within 6 years (3 for personal injury; 1 for penalties) "from the date when the
-- person ceased to be under a disability or died". (6)(c): for land or money charged on land, never after 30 years from
-- accrual. (s 2(2) is "subject to section 36(1)(b) of the Civil Law Act 1909", which bears on when a minor stops being under a
-- disability; it is not followed here.)
DECLARE Disability HAS
    `under disability when the right accrued` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years since disability ended` IS A NUMBER
    `personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A Disability
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disability extension saves the claim` IF
        `the person`'s `under disability when the right accrued`
    AND (IF `the person`'s `personal injury`
         THEN `the person`'s `years since disability ended` AT MOST 3
         ELSE `the person`'s `years since disability ended` AT MOST 6)

§§ `26 to 28 -- acknowledgment and part payment`

-- s 26(2): where a right to recover a debt or liquidated claim "has accrued" and the debtor "acknowledges the claim or makes any
-- payment in respect thereof, the right shall be deemed to have accrued on and not before the date of the acknowledgment or the
-- last payment". s 27(1): an acknowledgment must be IN WRITING and SIGNED. s 28(4): it binds the acknowledgor and successors
-- only; (6) a payment binds all persons liable; (5), (7) contemplate acknowledgments and payments made "after the expiration
-- of the period of limitation".
--
-- Nothing confines s 26 to claims still in time, and ss 28(5) and (7) assume it reaches expired ones: a signed "I owe you" or a
-- token payment in year 10 starts a fresh six years.
DECLARE Debt HAS
    `years since the last signed acknowledgment or payment` IS A NUMBER
    `years since accrual` IS A NUMBER
    `there has been a signed acknowledgment or payment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the acknowledgment was oral only` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the debt` IS A Debt
GIVETH A NUMBER
`years running` MEANS
    IF `the debt`'s `there has been a signed acknowledgment or payment` AND NOT `the debt`'s `the acknowledgment was oral only`
    THEN `the debt`'s `years since the last signed acknowledgment or payment`
    ELSE `the debt`'s `years since accrual`

GIVEN `the debt` IS A Debt
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the debt claim is in time` IF
    `years running` `the debt` AT MOST 6

§§ `29 -- fraud and mistake`

-- s 29(1): for an action based on the defendant's fraud, where the right is concealed by fraud, or for relief from mistake,
-- time "shall not begin to run until the claimant has discovered the fraud or the mistake ..., or could with reasonable
-- diligence have discovered it". (2): no recovery of property from a bona fide purchaser for value.
GIVEN `based on or concealed by fraud, or relief from mistake` IS A BOOLEAN, `years since discoverable` IS A NUMBER, `years since accrual` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`years counted` MEANS
    IF `based on or concealed by fraud, or relief from mistake` THEN `years since discoverable` ELSE `years since accrual`

§§ `35 -- the occupation years`

-- s 35: "In computing the period of limitation ..., the period commencing on 15 February 1942 and ending on 30 September 1949
-- shall be excluded." (The Japanese Occupation and the years after it.)
GIVEN `date as yyyymmdd` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the date falls in the excluded period` IF
    `date as yyyymmdd` AT LEAST 19420215 AND `date as yyyymmdd` AT MOST 19490930

§§ `33 -- taxes`

-- s 33(2): the Act does not apply to Government proceedings to recover any tax or duty, or to customs and excise forfeiture.
GIVEN `a Government tax or duty recovery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Limitation Act applies` IF
    NOT `a Government tax or duty recovery`
